<title>USA: USDA gross cutout hide and offal value.</title>
<headline>USDA gross cutout hide and offal value.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The hide and offal value from a typical slaughter steer for today was estimated at $9.17 per cwt live, down 0.01 when compared to Thursday's value.-USDA</p>
<p>FOB CENTRAL U.S. TODAY'S CALCULATIONS FOR BY-PRODUCT VALUE</p>
<p>(STEER) -			   Lbs   Price  Change   Value</p>
<p>Steer hide, butt brand	 5.07   89.00    -	 5.78</p>
<p>Tallow, edible		   1.20   19.00    -	 0.23</p>
<p>Tallow, packer bleachable    4.50   16.00    -	 0.72</p>
<p>Tongues, Swiss #1 Wht 0-3%   0.26  162.00    -	 0.42</p>
<p>Cheek meat, trmd		 0.32   65.00    -	 0.21</p>
<p>Head meat			  0.13   52.50    -	 0.07</p>
<p>Oxtail, selected		 0.16  160.50    -	 0.26</p>
<p>Hearts, reg, bone out	  0.38   24.00    -	 0.09</p>
<p>Lips, unscalded		  0.11   77.00    -	 0.08</p>
<p>Livers, slcted, gall off     0.96   40.00    -	 0.38</p>
<p>Tripe, scalded edible	  0.65   22.00    -	 0.14</p>
<p>Tripe, honeycomb bleached    0.15   38.00    -	 0.06</p>
<p>Lungs, inedible		  0.47    4.60    -	 0.02</p>
<p>Melts				0.14    6.25    -	 0.01</p>
<p>Meat bone ml, 50% blk/ton    3.70  277.50   -3.00    0.51</p>
<p>Blood meal, 85% blk/ton	0.60  621.50    -	 0.19</p>
<p>TOTAL :			   18.80			  9.17</p>
<p>The average value of hide and offal for the five days ending Friday, April 25, 1997 was estimated at 9.19 per cwt., down -0.07 from last week and up 0.89 from last year.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
